/* Bug #5781: "gcd with modulus set returns non-divisors and too small gcds, or hangs"
   More wrong gcds from gcd:spmod with modulus set, among them a candidate that divided only one of
   the polynomials and an evaluation point where both vanish. ZGCD picks random evaluation points,
   so each gcd is computed 20 times in each order. Under a modulus a correct gcd may come back times
   a constant, so results are compared up to one. */

(check_spmod_gcd(f, g, p, expected_result) :=
  block([gcds : block([gcd : spmod, modulus : p], append(makelist(gcd(f, g), 20), makelist(gcd(g, f), 20)))],
    if every(lambda([e], block([gcd : subres, modulus : p], numberp(ratdisrep(rat(e/expected_result))))), gcds)
    then true
    else FAILED_GCDS('modulus = p, 'expected = expected_result, 'actual = unique(gcds))),
  0);
0$

